Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||02-23-2000||01:53 AM||||well, since my stereo was not taken when the car was stolen, i guess i have to fix it...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> my RADIO works great, but when i play ANY tape or use a cd player w/ tape adapter, the sounds is so incredibly quiet that it is inaudible. i have tried head cleaning tapes a few times, but it didn't work. any ideas anyone?||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||02-23-2000||09:53 AM||||your sure the tape is moving? If it's actually moving and you can't hear it then the head may be out of alignment. It's likely easier to go to the yard ang get another radio then for most people to get the alignment right.<P>if the tape is not moving, like mine doesn't, the belt is shot.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||02-23-2000||11:13 AM||||Play a regular cassette tape that you know works ok and see what happens. If you need a new belt, Rodney Dickman sells these for $4 plus $1 for shipping.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroSTETZ||02-24-2000||11:31 PM||||if i turn the volume WAY up,  i can hear it playing, along with lots of static.. it is quiet enough that while playing a tape i cannot hear it if the car is running- but it IS playing! the normal radio plays at very good volume. i know the tapes i try are good because i try them out in my dad's car first||||reg||1
Z||000004||86SE||02-25-2000||12:16 AM||||I hade a AM/FM tape player raido in one of my cars once.  We installed a speaker or something w/o unhooking the battery, then, pop the raido goes out.......then i could turn the volume up ALL the way and just barly hear a wisper from the speakers.  Very little sound came out while playing the raido.  So if you still have good sound when the raido is on, your raido is still good, just maybe not your tape deck.||||reg||11
